  author: "Audi A1 Clubsport Quattro (https://skfb.ly/p9Cz7) by Mona x Supercars is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).",
  drivingExperience: "The CPTA (EA211 ACT) offers a unique driving experience. It delivers a punchy 140hp and 250Nm of torque, making it feel like a much larger engine. Under light load, it shuts off cylinders 2 and 3 seamlessly to save fuel, giving you hybrid-like efficiency on the highway. The switch is barely noticeable, but you might feel a slight resonance. It's incredibly agile due to the lightweight aluminum block.", mechanicVerdict: "A fantastic engine that blends performance and extreme efficiency. The core EA211 architecture is highly reliable with its belt drive. The ACT system is generally robust, though the actuators can sometimes leak oil. The biggest weakness remains the plastic water pump module. Keep the oil fresh to ensure the delicate ACT solenoids function properly.", repairCostEstimate: "$650 - $850 / year",
